	"description": "Firefox 155 watching a Chromium microphone publisher over a local relay, 20ms Opus, one frame per group. The receiver's own content process stopped executing for a few hundred milliseconds at a time while a Chromium watcher of the same broadcast over the same relay saw a worst reading gap of 46ms, so every gap in here is the receiver's rather than the path's, and each one is under the interval the spacing rule needs to discount it. The stalled flag marks the frames the recording can prove came out of a block: its debug sampler is a 250ms timer on the same main thread, so a firing more than 100ms late dates a block the way the player's own 50ms monitor does. That sampler cannot resolve a block that fits between two of its firings, so the marks are a lower bound and the target this settles on is still above the 40ms the path asked for.",
